PASS  slow: the call reached the slow server, and get returned at once
PASS  slow: another client is answered by the program meanwhile
PASS  slow: and through a second upstream
PASS  slow: both inside the slow call's deadline
PASS  slow: the slow call ends UPSTREAM_E_TIMEOUT and its client gets a 504
PASS  slow: its slot and connection are given back
PASS  keep-alive: five calls in a row are answered, each tagged with its request
PASS  keep-alive: on one connection
PASS  keep-alive: the request head is the path and the origin's Host
PASS  refusal: a malformed status line fails the call with code 1
PASS  refusal: a bare LF fails the call with code 3
PASS  refusal: conflicting framing fails the call with code 6
PASS  refusal: a body past maxBody fails the call with code 14
PASS  refusal: a body cut short fails the call with code 10
PASS  refusal: the next call is answered on a new connection
PASS  policy: a loopback origin is refused at start-up
PASS  policy: and each call fails UPSTREAM_E_BLOCKED with nothing connected
PASS  policy: permitted, the same origin is called
PASS  origin: https, userinfo and a path are each UPSTREAM_E_ORIGIN
PASS  request: a path that is not a request target is UPSTREAM_E_REQUEST
PASS  warm pool: three thousand calls are answered
PASS  warm pool: on the one connection, with every slot back and no body buffer grown
PASS  warm pool: Arena.used() flat over two thousand calls past a thousand of warm-up
PASS  idle: a connection the origin closed while idle is not reused, and the next call is answered
PASS  idle: bytes the origin sent while the connection was idle are not the next call's response
PASS  retry: a call the origin drops unanswered on a reused connection is made once more on a new one
PASS  reset: a close-delimited body ends at the origin's close
PASS  reset: a reset in a close-delimited body fails the call UPSTREAM_E_RESET, not ok with what came
PASS  connections: three calls with one connection allowed share it, one after another
PASS  request: an absolute-form or asterisk path is UPSTREAM_E_REQUEST, with nothing sent
PASS  calls: with every slot taken, get answers UPSTREAM_E_FULL and holds nothing
PASS  calls: once the slot is released, get takes a call again
PASS  request: a request head past maxHead is UPSTREAM_E_REQUEST, with nothing sent
PASS  request: and one that fits is called
PASS  policy: a host name the policy does not allow is refused before any lookup
PASS  late reply: a call past its deadline fails UPSTREAM_E_TIMEOUT and its connection is closed
PASS  late reply: the next call gets its own response, on a new connection
